READ(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    read - read a line into shell variables

SYNOPSIS
    read [-r] [name...]

DESCRIPTION
    Reads one line from stdin. Fields are separated using IFS; the last name
    receives the remaining fields. With no names, stores the line in REPLY.
    Backslash escapes the next character unless -r is used; backslash-newline
    continues a line. Returns 1 on EOF, including a final unterminated line.
    Example: read first rest <<EOF
                 hello two words
             EOF

SEE ALSO
    sh(1), man(1), index(7)
